# Copy to .env and fill in per-machine values before `docker compose up`.

# REQUIRED — absolute HOST filesystem path to python-counting/ (this repo's
# sibling dir, NOT the dashboard container's own /python-counting mount path).
# The dashboard container talks to the HOST's Docker daemon via the mounted
# docker.sock to run triton-model-builder / yolo-export as sibling containers;
# those need the HOST path to resolve their own -v mounts correctly. If this
# is missing or wrong, Docker silently bind-mounts an EMPTY directory instead
# and builds fail with confusing "file not found" errors for scripts that do
# exist — see lib/compose.ts checkHostMountConfig(). Every machine that runs
# this dashboard needs its own correct value here, e.g.:
#   HOST_PYTHON_COUNTING_DIR=/opt/ai/dashboard-python-counting/python-counting
HOST_PYTHON_COUNTING_DIR=/absolute/host/path/to/python-counting

# Optional overrides — defaults already work for the standard docker-compose
# setup (dashboard + triton on the shared "envisions" network); only set
# these for a non-docker dev run or a non-default Triton container name.
# TRITON_HTTP_URL=http://triton-inference-server:8000
# TRITON_METRICS_URL=http://triton-inference-server:8002
# SETTINGS_FILE=/app/data/settings.json
# FACE_PHOTO_DIR=/app/data/face-photos
